<p class="lead">Readers should be able to trust what they read here. These principles guide every story we publish.</p>

<h2>Accuracy</h2>
<p>We verify facts before publishing and attribute information to its source. When something is unconfirmed, we say so.</p>

<h2>Review before publication</h2>
<p>Every article written by an author is reviewed by an editor. Editors can approve an article, or return it to the author with a note explaining what needs to change. Only approved articles are published.</p>

<h2>Independence</h2>
<p>Editorial decisions are made by the newsroom. We separate news reporting from opinion and clearly label breaking news.</p>

<h2>Corrections</h2>
<p>When we make a mistake, we correct it promptly and update the article's modified date. To report an error, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>

<h2>Comments</h2>
<p>Registered readers can comment on published stories. We remove comments that are abusive, off-topic or unlawful.</p>
